<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 2.2 pct in March - Istat. [CORRECTED 07:38 GMT]</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 2.2 pct in March - Istat. [CORRECTED 07:38 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	   March 97    Feb 97     March 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.1	  0.1	  0.3</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     2.2	  2.4	  4.5</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    105.3	105.2	103.0</p>
<p>(Corrects February 1997 year-on-year inflation figure from 2.3 pct to 2.4 pct.)</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 2.2 percent for March.  </p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tobacco)     104.1	   -0.1	   1.1</p>
<p> Clothing			 106.2	    0.2	   2.9</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel   108.8	    0.4	   5.5</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 105.1	    0.1	   1.9</p>
<p> Health spending		105.5	    0.1	   3.0</p>
<p> Transport			106.0	    0.3	   2.2</p>
<p> Recreation		     103.4	   -0.4	   0.8</p>
<p> Education			107.5	    0.1	   3.8</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  105.9	    0.2	   2.9</p>
<p> Other goods,services	 103.6	    0.3	   0.8</p>
<p>(including communications)</p>
</text>
